Package: kstitch
Title: Integrating Cell Morphology and Gene Expression in Spatial Transcriptomics
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    c(person("Vishaka", "Gopalan", role = c("aut", "cre"),
             email = "vishaka.gopalan@nih.gov"),
      person("Shashwat", "Kumar", role = "aut"))
Description: A framework for identifying interpretable covariation between cell
    or nuclear morphology and gene expression in imaging-based spatial
    transcriptomics data. Represents contour shape using tangent principal
    component analysis (TPCA) in Kendall shape space, models gene-expression
    programs using non-negative matrix factorization (NMF), and links the two
    modalities using canonical correlation analysis (CCA). Designed to work
    with Seurat v5 objects and boundary data from platforms such as Xenium
    and CosMx.
